🟡 Variables and Memory Concept

python automatically decides type, can directly take a vairable and assign a value to it
for example: 
x = 10
name = "my-name"

Variables naming conventions
✅ : age, age1, age_1, _age, a1g1e1 (start with alphabet or underscore, underscore or numric allowed after an alphabet)
❌ : @ge, 1age, 1_age (No starting with numbers, no inclusion of special characters) 


🟡Taking user input

input() method to take input from a user
for example: 
name = input("Enter your name: ")
print("Hello", name)

📌(input method always returns a string, so might need to convert as per usecase or to perform calculations)